---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const stats = [
  { label: "Resources listed", value: "80+", detail: "Local services in our directory" },
  { label: "Service categories", value: "12", detail: "Food, shelter, health, housing, recovery, and more" },
  { label: "Coverage area", value: "Brevard County", detail: "Brevard County focus, county-wide directory" },
  { label: "Languages", value: "Any", detail: "Use your browser's translate feature" },
];
---

<Base title="Impact — Base Impact" description="The impact Base Impact is making in Brevard County, FL — technology access, digital skills, and community support.">
  <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-semibold text-body mb-4 fade-in">Impact</h1>
  <div class="space-y-8">
    <p class="max-w-2xl text-muted leading-relaxed">
      Base Impact is a young organization making a real difference in Brevard County.
      Here's what we're building and the impact we're having.
    </p>

    <section class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-4 stagger-children">
      {stats.map((stat) => (
        <div class="rounded-2xl bg-card p-5 text-center shadow-[var(--shadow-border)]">
          <p class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-accent">{stat.value}</p>
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-body mt-1">{stat.label}</p>
          <p class="text-xs text-faint mt-1">{stat.detail}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </section>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-body mt-6">What we're building</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-muted leading-relaxed">
      <li><strong>Resource directory</strong> — A simpler, local starting point for finding food, shelter, health, housing, and recovery services. Works alongside 211.</li>
      <li><strong>Technology access</strong> — Helping neighbors get working devices and internet service.</li>
      <li><strong>Digital skills</strong> — Walk-throughs for housing portals, job applications, benefits, and staying safe online.</li>
      <li><strong>Nonprofit tech support</strong> — Free setup, security, and support for small community groups.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-body mt-6">How we measure impact</h2>
    <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed">
      We track the resources people find, the organizations we help, and the skills people learn.
      Our goal is simple: more neighbors connected, more nonprofits supported.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-body mt-6">AI &amp; technology grants</h2>
    <p>Base Impact is pursuing technology grants and partnerships to bring AI-powered tools to the community:</p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-muted leading-relaxed">
      <li><strong>AI form filling assistant</strong> — Local AI that helps people complete government forms, job applications, and housing applications without cloud dependency.</li>
      <li><strong>AI document reader for seniors</strong> — AI-powered tool that reads and summarizes documents, medical bills, and legal notices for elderly residents.</li>
      <li><strong>AI resource finder</strong> — Chatbot that connects people to local resources (food, shelter, jobs, healthcare) based on their needs.</li>
      <li><strong>AI job search assistant</strong> — Helps people write resumes, practice interviews, and find employment.</li>
      <li><strong>AI translation service</strong> — Real-time translation for non-English speakers at community events.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-sm text-faint">All AI runs locally — no data leaves the device. This protects privacy for vulnerable community members.</p>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-body mt-6">Technology grant targets</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-muted leading-relaxed">
      <li><strong>Florida State Digital Equity Grant</strong> — Workforce development, digital literacy, device ownership.</li>
      <li><strong>NCOA Digital Literacy Grant</strong> — Digital skills training for adults 60+ (AT&T funded).</li>
      <li><strong>Mobile Beacon Wi-Fly Grant</strong> — $20,000+ in donated technology and internet access.</li>
      <li><strong>NTIA Digital Equity Competitive Grant</strong> — $1.25B program, reopening December 2026.</li>
      <li><strong>Google for Nonprofits</strong> — $10,000/month Ad Grants + free Workspace + cloud credits.</li>
      <li><strong>Microsoft for Nonprofits</strong> — $2,000/year Azure credits + discounted software.</li>
      <li><strong>TechSoup</strong> — 50-90% off hardware and software for nonprofits.</li>
      <li><strong>PCs for People</strong> — Refurbished computers and tablets at low cost.</li>
      <li><strong>AWS Imagine Grant</strong> — Cloud credits + cash grants for AI/cloud projects.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-body mt-6">Infrastructure goals</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-muted leading-relaxed">
      <li><strong>AI-capable hardware</strong> — Acquire laptops and workstations to run local AI models for form filling, document understanding, and technology troubleshooting. No cloud dependency, no data leaving the device.</li>
      <li><strong>Training devices</strong> — Laptops and tablets for hands-on digital skills training sessions. Devices may be loaned or donated to participants.</li>
      <li><strong>Cell phone partnerships</strong> — Partner with cellular providers (AT&T, Verizon, T-Mobile) to provide free or low-cost phones and tablets to homeless individuals and people in need.</li>
      <li><strong>Tech company partnerships</strong> — Tablets, laptops, computers, parts, and servers from technology companies for NPO use and AI generation.</li>
      <li><strong>Church &amp; nonprofit partnerships</strong> — Collaborations with local churches and nonprofits for events, programs, and projects.</li>
      <li><strong>Device refurbishment</strong> — Establish a device refurbishment program to extend the life of donated technology.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-body mt-6">Community need</h2>
    <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed">
      Brevard County has limited access to technology support for vulnerable populations.
      Many neighbors lack reliable internet, working devices, or the digital skills needed to
      access housing, jobs, healthcare, and benefits. Small nonprofits serving these communities
      often operate with minimal technology resources.
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm text-faint">Base Impact is a pre-filing nonprofit in Scottsmoor, FL. We're just getting started.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
